Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a candidate query lost in the medium is resent with its MID, each query logged

An Unassociated STA Link Metrics Query whose CMDU (or its reply) is lost was answered by
nothing: the controller keeps one outstanding MID per radio and only its 10 s command time limit
ended it, after em_cli's 8 s candidate wait had already given up (HTTP 504). On the K8's lab
(rdk-1009, 9 to 10 October) rf-actions/clear failed this way in 2 of 4 runs, the query lost in
a burst of hwsim drops on the extenders the test loaded, where a reply normally comes in 55 ms.

The query as sent is kept with its MID, and resent unchanged while unanswered 2 s and 4.5 s
after the first send (twice at most, within em_cli's wait and the command's time limit), from
the orchestration's 250 ms tick. A copy with the same MID is the same request: the agent's
tracker accepts it again and measures (or answers the measurement in flight), and EMOSA's
agents answer each copy; a reply is matched only to a radio still waiting with that MID, so a
second reply after the first completed the query is ignored ("uncorrelated"), never matched
to another query.

Each candidate query now has an INFO line when it starts (MID, agent, radio), for each resend,
and when it ends (answered, rejected or expired, with its resends and time): what was in
flight when a later query is refused is in the log.

Platform-independent; for the lab's candidate measurements, upstream once proven.

Upstream-Status: Pending

